From 4c5ad160b8fa200809309ac7871e796438d11cd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: box <box@localhost>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:39:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] session: read a prebuilt focal32.mbn, use the in-tree
 focaltech-fp driver, no uname

- fp5_fw.c: load <dir>/focal32.mbn first (droid-juicer squashes the
  trustlet to /var/lib/firmware/qsee/focal32.mbn on BengalOS), fall back
  to .mdt + .b00..bNN assembled in memory. Directory: $FP5_QTEE_FW_DIR,
  else the argument, else /var/lib/firmware/qsee, then /lib/firmware/qsee.
  Segment count comes from the files present, not a fixed 8. Unit test.
- fp5-qtee-load --assemble DIR OUT writes the in-memory image to a file
  (no TEE), for a byte compare with droid-juicer's focal32.mbn.
- Sensor backend chosen by feature checks: the in-tree focaltech-fp
  driver (firmware_name attribute; /dev/focaltech_fp read()/poll(), the fd
  is kept open because the driver disarms on the last close) or the old
  focaltech_fp_life module (sysfs). The module is loaded with modprobe or
  $FP5_FP_LIFE_KO, never from a /lib/modules/$(uname -r) path.
- FP5_QTEE_MOUNT_PERSIST=0 stops the session from mounting persist itself.

Builds with gcc (host) and aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc (glibc). Untested on
the phone.
